WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.640
It is no secret

2
00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.370
that we love all things design

3
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.203
on this show.

4
00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:05.850
I wanted it to be a big part of this show

5
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.600
'cause it's a big part of my life.

6
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.990
So when we heard the design dilemma of our next guest

7
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.970
we were excited to help create a brand new segment,

8
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.117
we're calling Design Court.

9
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:18.565
(gavel clacks)
(audience cheers)

10
00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:20.150
Both sides will state their cases.

11
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.900
And by end of this trial,

12
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.265
we will reach a design verdict.

13
00:00:23.265 --> 00:00:24.098
(gavel clacks)

14
00:00:24.098 --> 00:00:25.658
Yeah!
(audience cheers)

15
00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.393
Take a look at the Philpott's design dilemma.

16
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.770 line:15%
Hi Drew, my name is Cass.

17
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.980 line:15%
My name is Ted and we're the Philpotts.

18
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.210 line:15%
We are hoping that you can help us

19
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.540
settle a design issue in our home.

20
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.870
Basically we've been in this house

21
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.240
for about 15 years.

22
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.150
We have redone all the other rooms

23
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.350
to suit our lifestyle.

24
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.817
With the exception of this one.

25
00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:48.540
The room is called the back 40

26
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.700
because it tends to be the catchall for the house.

27
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.130
And I would like to see it be more of a tranquil space

28
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.750
a quiet place to escape everything from the house.

29
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.080
Clean lines, quiet colors, calm furniture,

30
00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.950
and a place just to retreat.

31
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.950
What I'd like to do

32
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.170
is something a little bit more entertainment style,

33
00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.220
pub style, game room style, theater style.

34
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.800
So maybe a big TV, a shuffleboard table, some large couches.

35
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.960
Something comfortable for myself, our friends,

36
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.470
my daughter and her friends

37
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.880
to hang out and relax a little bit.

38
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:20.977
So a day in the life of the Philpotts,

39
00:01:20.977 --> 00:01:22.410
you see we don't agree.

40
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.883
So we need help.

41
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.210
(audience cheers)

42
00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.160
Well, we could not start a trial

43
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.710
without Drew Crew member

44
00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.291
and my partner in crime of design, Mikel Welch.

45
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:34.338
Hey friend!

46
00:01:34.338 --> 00:01:35.950
(audience cheers)

47
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.310
Good to see you again.

48
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:40.080
I hate the idea of working against you.

49
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.420
Usually we're a team.

50
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.610
I know, but you know what,

51
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.320
a little fun banter never hurt.

52
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.700
Let's do this.
Let's do it.

53
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.940
All right, well, it is time to meet our design litigants

54
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.690
Cass and Ted Philpott.

55
00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.818
Come on out!

56
00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:54.111
(audience cheers)

57
00:01:54.111 --> 00:01:57.486
(dramatic music)

58
00:01:57.486 --> 00:01:58.486
Hi, hello!

59
00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:04.080
Well, Design Court is now in session.

60
00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.020
Uh-oh.

61
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.210
All right, Mikel is representing Ted

62
00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.370
and I will be representing Cass.

63
00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.650
Now, Cass, let's start with your opening statement.

64
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.170
Please address the court with your vision for the room.

65
00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.330
So we have such crazy busy lives as it is

66
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.550
that I feel like our home should be our sanctuary

67
00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.360 line:15%
and we should have a space to retreat

68
00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.030 line:15%
from all the togetherness.

69
00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.550 line:15%
So I would like to see the room,

70
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:32.360
be a design that's for solitude, peace,

71
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.930
and just some alone time.

72
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.390
And is it correct that you read

73
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.780
two to three books a week?

74
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.100
I do.
Possibly a day.

75
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.340
Oh wow.

76
00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.610
I am an avid reader.

77
00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.740
Do you hear that Mikel?

78
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.162
I heard it.

79
00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:45.995
I heard it.

80
00:02:45.995 --> 00:02:47.290
All right.
I heard it.

81
00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.020
Ted, state your case?

82
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.550
She's not wrong.

83
00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.350
Our life is hectic and she has a beautiful, comfortable room

84
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.230 line:15%
in the living room and the bedroom

85
00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:59.310 line:15%
and the patio outside to read plenty of books

86
00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.450 line:15%
as long as she wants to.

87
00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.710
That's a lot of room.

88
00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.690
Right, we also do a lot of entertaining

89
00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.724
and we need a space

90
00:03:05.724 --> 00:03:08.060
that brings a little bit of life to the house.

91
00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.010
Some sort of game room,

92
00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.940 line:15%
someplace where our younger daughter

93
00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:11.950 line:15%
and her friends can hang out.

94
00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.930 line:15%
Someplace I can unwind and kind of get away

95
00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.440 line:15%
from the hectic life that she's trying to escape.

96
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.770 line:15%
Well, I thank you, councils

97
00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.440
for excellent opening statements.

98
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.660
Good arguments.

99
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.809
Well, the jury is still out.

100
00:03:21.809 --> 00:03:24.392 line:15%
(upbeat music)

